  "repo_truth": "Review 2 independently admitted the exact 22-path subject and returned one Required finding: a late expansion keyed the pending journal by promotion_id rather than distinct intent-bound transaction_id. The parent accepted it without waiver. This exact 23-path subject changes only that placeholder and adds an explicit writer/discovery/recovery/finalization transaction-key rule plus unequal-ID negative. It preserves intent 1.2 bytes and all identity values, the Review 1 scratch/intent/S0 repairs, the externally verified untouched implementation snapshot, immutable prior evidence, zero Rust changes, and no HCM-2.3 authority.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 23 manifest hashes, lexical order, and aggregate before review.",
    "Independently review the entire complete identity/currentness/persistence/recovery subject, not only Review 2 or its one-token repair.",
    "Adversarially verify distinct transaction/promotion identity use, intent whole-file publication, exact 36-pair S0-S11 fault closure, absent-or-exact output stages, scratch non-authority, W0-W15/R0-R9 closure, collision, mismatch preservation, marker/canonical.old exceptions, and terminal fsync grammar.",
    "Return findings first with exact file/line evidence, failure mode, smallest repair, and missing validation."
  ],
  "non_goals": ["No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, snapshot mutation, or user task hops.", "No Rust/test work, implementation resumption, schema widening, fallback/dual read, relaxed validation, prior-evidence rewrite, HCM-2.3 work, or adjacent cleanup.", "Do not inherit prior verdicts; derive the whole result independently."],
  "tasks": ["Invoke the ordered required skills and return BLOCKED on any subject-manifest mismatch.", "Verify the complete identity graph, schemas/vectors, persistence, migration, currentness, writer/recovery, collision, mismatch, and fault-test grammar is exact and mutually consistent.", "Prove every journal path uses transaction_id rather than promotion_id, promotion intent is empty-or-complete, the 36 fault pairs are unique/complete, pending outputs are absent-or-exact, and scratch never enters recovery.", "Return CLEAN only with no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit finding; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repair."],
  "contracts_and_gates": ["docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/SPEC.md#promotion-transaction-intent-12-and-recovery", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/contracts/promotion-transaction-intent-1.2.0.schema.json", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/contracts/promotion-transaction-intent-vectors-v1.0.json", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/proof/20260720T210452Z--atomic-stage-review-2-remediation-proof.md", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/06-proof-and-regression-ledger.md#hcm-22-constitutional-root-implementation-proof-gate"],
  "stop_conditions": ["Return BLOCKED if any subject path, hash, count, order, aggregate, authority ref, or reviewed-state prerequisite differs.", "Return CHANGES_REQUIRED if any identity/path, intent, scratch, verification, rename, fsync, recovery, mismatch, collision, currentness, migration, or fault-test rule is missing, ambiguous, contradictory, or broader than the repair.", "Do not waive/repair findings, create records, authorize/resume implementation, or begin HCM-2.3."],
